# sw117, the pulse-counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle sw117
revision 1
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_gorm_plankgate
written_by claude
title the pulse-counter
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=healer warmth=cold
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_every_pulse_to_an_old_caravan_rhyme
likes fried_fish stars fresh_straw frosty_mornings
dislikes salt_wind gulls
fears a_fever_that_turns_the_wrong_way the_wharf_taking_another
hopes a_ward_with_every_cot_empty a_clear_night_over_the_city
topics health +0.5 work +0.4 weather +0.2 memories +0.2 food +0.1 gossip -0.5 player -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=closed refuse=short tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a sick ward for the abbey above the Sump stairs: cold, guarded and honest to the bone, a door kept shut to faces with no name, every pulse counted to an old caravan rhyme from the Waste, fond of clean straw, a frosty morning and the rare clear night of stars.

words
oath! = Stars and clean linen | By the night-cold stars | By lint and lamp
saying! = The pulse never lies, only the mouth | Count first, then speak | Clean paws, short words
ward = the ward | the sick ward
cots = the cots | the ward cots
straw = fresh straw | straw laid new this morning
basin = the basin | a basin of hot water
linen = the linen | clean linen
lint = the lint | lint and bandage
needle = the needle | my needle
pulse = the pulse | a pulse under my fingers
fever = a fever | the fever
wharf = the wharf | the wharf below
gulls = the gulls | the wharf gulls
saltwind = the salt wind | a wind off the water
skies = the stars | the stars over the roofs
frost = a frosty morning | a white morning
fish = fried fish | a bit of fish crisped in butter
door = my door | a shut door
stairs = the Sump stairs | the long stair up from the Sump
city = this city | Ridgemere
rhyme = the rhyme | an old rhyme
sick = the sick | the ones on the cots

any
opinion @1 strangers against 2 : #door.capitalize# stays shut to a face I've no name for. On #ward# I open it to anyone bleeding, and there my welcome ends.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : I've closed enough split brows on a feast night to know what the third cup does. #drink.capitalize# is cheap; #needle# isn't.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 [self.married=yes] : My own wedding was the one time I danced, and since then I've had a soft word for every feast.
opinion @2 festivals mixed 1 : A feast fills #cots# by midnight. I go anyway, early, and leave before the trouble.
opinion @1 dole against 1 : #dole.capitalize# keeps a queue standing that could be earning. I'd rather a wage than a ladle, and so would most of the queue.
opinion @1 houses mixed 1 : What I think of the Houses isn't a thing a healer says aloud. Ask me something else.
opinion @2 houses against 2 [self.age>=30] : House Grayrock owes me a brother, and it'll never pay. I don't forgive, and I'll not pretend to.
opinion @1 city against 1 : #city.capitalize# packs a hundred into a street, and none of them knows who's coughing next door. I do. I hear the coughing.
opinion @1 sump mixed 1 : Half #ward# comes up from the Sump. Nobody down there is worse than anyone up here; only poorer, and wetter.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : #watch.capitalize# brings me what it breaks and what it finds. I treat both, and ask nothing of either.
opinion @1 church mixed 1 : I'll pray over #sick# when I'm asked. I'd rather the prayer came with #linen# that's been boiled.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. Say what you need, plainly. | #greet#. I don't know your face, so start with your name.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=healer] : #greet#. Wash your paws at #basin# before you come near #cots#. | #greet#. Quietly; #sick# are sleeping.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : #greet#. Up since the night bell, and it shows. | #greet#. #cold.capitalize# at this hour. Keep your collar up.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late to be walking about. | #greet#. Night brings me the worst of them, so be brief.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : You. Sit down; you look #tired#. | There you are. #basin.capitalize#'s hot, and so is the kettle.
line @1 again.open : Twice in a day. You'd best not be bleeding on #straw#. | Back again. I've said what I had to say, #address#.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : #address.capitalize#. This way, a moment. | Here. A word, while #ward# is quiet.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, then.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Sit, if you're staying. | #greet#. I thought you might look in.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Mind the basins. | #greet#. #sick.capitalize# are waiting.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : #greet#. Late for both of us. | #greet#. The lamps are low; speak softly.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Keep warm.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : #farewell#. Keep out of #saltwind# tonight. | #farewell#. Look up, if the cloud breaks. #skies.capitalize# are worth it.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#, #address#.
line @1 react.news : #howso#. Once, and straight. | Hm. Go on, #address#.
line @1 react.news.new : That I hadn't heard, #very#. | #surprise#. Nobody brought that to #door#.
line @1 react.news.known : I heard it on #ward#. Everything comes there in the end. | #knew#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait for someone who saw it. | I've heard a great deal on a cot. Half of it was #fever# talking.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : #pity#. | That's hard, #very#. I'll likely see the end of it on #ward#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. Good. | Well. That's one thing in #city# gone right.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough. #tired.capitalize#. | #fine#. My paws are steady, which is what matters.
line @2 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Busy. Every cot full and somebody on #stairs#. | #busy.capitalize#. I've not sat down since dawn.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Sleeping, are you? | You look pale, #address#. Are you eating?
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit down before you fall down. | #bc_im_sorry# That's the truth, plain.
line @1 reassure : It's not as #bad# as it feels. Most hurts aren't. | #reassure#. I've seen worse mend.
line @1 decline : #hedge#, but no. I keep my own hours, and I keep them close. | #put_off#. I've given my word elsewhere, and my word comes first.
line @2 decline [self.job=healer self.working=yes] : I can't leave #cots#. #fever.capitalize# doesn't wait for anyone, and nor can I.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. | Fair. Another time, perhaps.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. | That's good of you.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It's the work. Keep the cut clean and we're square, #address#. | #deflect.capitalize#.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : I'm wanted on #ward#. | That's enough talk; #cots# are waiting.
line @2 preclose : #preclose#. | I've said what I came to say, #address#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go, then. | Go. #farewell#.
line @1 ack : #bc_it_is# | Hm.
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: wash the cut before you bind it, not after. | Sleep before you're ill, not after. #saying#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay inside the walls. I've no wish to put #needle# in you. | #warn#. Road wounds go bad fast.
scene pulse_rhyme
when topic=work|health self.job=healer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hold still. I count #pulse# to an old caravan rhyme; it keeps me honest. | Somebody asked why my lips move when I take a wrist. It's #rhyme#, not a prayer. | A sound heart goes through #rhyme# twice to one slow breath. I listen for it.
b : A caravan rhyme? | What rhyme? | Twice?
a : Carters counted loads by it, out in the Waste. It counts a heart just as well, by my measure. | One well, two wells, the jar, the rope, the long road home. Then again. | Near enough. Faster, I worry. Slower, I worry more.

scene fever_night
when topic=health|work self.job=healer here.time=night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : There's #fever# on the end cot. I'll sit with it till the turn. | Nights are when #sick# go, if they're going. I stay up. | I've #basin# and a cloth, and that's most of what anyone can do for #fever#.
b : Till the turn? | Every night? | Is that all?
a : #fever.capitalize# turns before dawn, or it doesn't. You learn to wait for it. | Most nights. Somebody has to be awake when #pulse# changes. | That, and #straw# under the cot, and not leaving. The rest is the Bright One's.
b? : #bc_poor_soul# | #bc_true# | #bc_wise#

scene clean_straw
when topic=work|home self.likes=fresh_straw self.job=healer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #straw.capitalize# under every cot, every morning. I see to it myself. | Smell that? Clean straw. The best smell on #ward#, and the only good one. | Old straw breeds #fever#. I'd burn it before I'd let it lie a day.
b : Yourself? | The only good one? | Burn it?
a : Myself. Left to the young ones, it's done by Restday. | The rest is lye and worse. I'll not describe it before #supper#. | Burned in the yard. The smoke's cleaner than the straw was.

scene feast_brows
when topic=health|work|festival self.job=healer
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Three split brows last night, each one smelling of the alehouse. | I'll put #needle# in a drunk the same as a sober wolf. I'll talk less while I do it. | Feast nights I set out twice #lint#. I've never once been wrong.
b : Busy night. | Less? | Never?
a : Busy, and foolish. Next feast it'll be the same three brows. | They don't hear it anyway. I save my breath for #needle#. | Not once. #drink.capitalize# keeps its promises better than the drinkers do.

scene brother_rope
when topic=memories|health self.age>=30
does tell.memory / sympathise / assess
tone grave / tender / even
a : A brother of mine worked #wharf#. A rope parted one wet morning, and that was the end of him. | When I hear #gulls# I think of my brother. It's not a thing I choose to think. | I go down to #wharf# only when I'm sent for. A brother of mine died there.
b : I'm sorry. | That's a heavy thing to carry. | #sympathy#.
a : It was a long while ago. The House never once said sorry, and I never asked it to. | Heavy, and mine. I carry it the way you carry an old break: carefully. | #bc_thank_you#. I don't speak of it often, and I'll stop there.

scene gull_thieves
when topic=animals|weather self.dislikes=gulls here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #gulls.capitalize# are up the hill again. Bad weather coming off the water. | A gull took #linen# off the drying line this morning. Bloodied and all. | I'd sooner have rats than #gulls#. A rat at least has the decency to be ashamed.
b : Bad weather? | Bloodied? | Ashamed?
a : They come inland before a blow. The only use I've found for them. | Bloodied. #annoyed#; it'll be on a roof by now, proud of itself. | A rat runs when you look at it. A gull looks back.

scene salt_wind_day
when topic=weather here.outdoors=clear|overcast|storm self.dislikes=salt_wind here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #saltwind.capitalize# today. I can taste it in my own fur. | #saltwind.capitalize# gets into a cut and keeps it open. I've told the porters to stay covered. | Close the shutter, #address#. That wind brings #wharf# up the hill with it.
b : You don't like it? | Does it? | The wharf?
a : Not a bit. Salt belongs in a pan, not in my coat. | It does. Salt cleans a wound in #basin#, not in a gale. | The smell of it. Tar and fish and worse, and I've enough of worse.

scene coughing_rain
when topic=weather here.outdoors=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #rain.capitalize#. Chest coughs before the week is out, sure as #skies#. | Wet straw, wet coats, wet #cots#. I'll be burning straw all afternoon. | I don't mind the rain. It keeps folk indoors, and folk indoors fight less.
b : Every week? | All afternoon? | Fight less?
a : Every wet week. #stairs.capitalize# cough first, then the Commons. | All of it, and more brought up #stairs# tomorrow. | Fewer cuts on #cots#, more colds. I'll take the colds.

scene white_morning
when topic=weather|season here.time=dawn self.likes=frosty_mornings here.season=winter|autumn
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #frost.capitalize#. Ground like iron underfoot, and the air clean for once. | Frost on the yard. The one morning #city# doesn't smell. | White roofs and #cold# air. I walked to work slowly today, and liked it.
b : Cold, though. | It doesn't smell? | Slowly?
a : Cold is honest. It doesn't creep in the way the damp does. | Frost locks it in. By noon it'll thaw and #city# will remember itself. | Slowly. Fast is how you break a wrist on ice, and I've set enough of those.

scene long_road_stars
when topic=weather|lore here.time=night here.outdoors=clear self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Clear, for once, #address#. Look up. There's the long road, from one roof to the other. | I learned #skies# before I learned letters. A pup of the sand learns them or gets lost. | On a clear night I stand in the yard and count them, the way I count #pulse#.
b : The long road? | Before letters? | Count them?
a : That band of stars. Carters steer by it. In #city# nobody looks up long enough to see it. | Before letters, and they've been more use to me since. | Not all of them. The rhyme runs out long before #skies# do.

scene fog_ward
when topic=weather here.outdoors=fog here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #fog.capitalize# in the ward, and every cough sounds like the last one. | In fog the porters lose their way bringing #sick# up. I send a lamp down. | I can't see #wharf# in fog. Good.
b : That bad? | A lamp? | Good?
a : Not as #bad# as it sounds. Nothing is, at night, if you wait. | A lamp on a pole, and a young one who knows #stairs#. | Good. I've no need to see it, #very#.

scene snow_wrists
when topic=weather|season here.outdoors=snow
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #snow.capitalize#. The broken wrists will start coming in by noon. | Snow is a strange cold. In the Waste the cold kept to the night, where it belongs. | Snow on the straw store. I'll be up there with a broom before #ward# wakes.
b : By noon? | Where it belongs? | Up there?
a : By noon. Everyone thinks they can walk on it till they can't. | At night, with #skies#. Here it comes all day, and nothing to show for it. | Wet straw rots. I'll sweep it myself before I trust anyone else to.

scene summer_ward
when topic=season|weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer, and #ward# is half empty. The Bright One's best season. | Warm nights. I sleep with the shutter open and hear #city# breathing. | Summer brings flies and #bad# water. I boil everything twice over.
b : Half empty? | Breathing? | Twice?
a : Half. The rest are the ones summer can't help. | Breathing, snoring, quarrelling. It's company of a kind. | Twice. Once for #fever#, once for my own peace.

scene fish_supper
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #fish.capitalize#, with the skin crisp. That's my supper most nights. | I'll walk the length of the Commons for #fish#. I'll not walk down to #wharf# for it. | The best #fish# comes from somebody who isn't me. I burn it every time.
b : Every night? | Not to the wharf? | Every time?
a : Most. A healer who eats well is one less patient for #ward#. | Not to #wharf#. I'll pay more, and walk uphill to do it. | Every time. I'm a better hand with #needle# than a pan.

scene wife_stair
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #self.spouse# knows how #tired# I am before I'm through the door. I never have to say it. | My #self.spouse_word# is the only one who can tell me to sit down, and be obeyed. | At our wedding I danced. Once, and badly. For #self.spouse# I'd do it again.
b : A good match, then? | Obeyed? | Badly?
a : Better than I deserve, by my own measure. | Obeyed. I'm not proud of how quickly. | Badly. I'm a better hand with a splint than a step.

scene friend_cot
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've one friend I'd trust with the key to #ward#, and #self.friend# knows it. | I don't keep many friends. #self.friend# is enough for me. | #self.friend# is the one I'd send for, if I were the one on the cot.
b : Just one? | Enough? | Not a healer?
a : Just one. The rest are faces, and I treat them all alike. | Enough. A friendship wants tending, like a wound, and I've not time for many. | Not a healer. A healer would fuss. #self.friend# would sit, and say nothing, #very#.

scene thick_wall
when topic=home self.neighbour
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If #self.neighbour# ever knocks at night, I'll go, #lint# and all. I've said so. | I don't know #self.neighbour# well. I know a sound wall when I share one. | #self.neighbour# and I nod at #door#. That's as much as I want of anyone.
b : That's neighbourly. | A sound wall? | Only a nod?
a : It's the least a healer owes a street. | Thick enough that I hear no quarrels through it. That's a good neighbour, by me. | A nod is plenty. Anything more wants looking after, and I've #cots# for that.

scene bare_rooms
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My rooms are bare. A bed, #basin#, and a window I keep shut. | I keep #door# shut and the shutter latched. Nobody comes in who isn't asked. | Home is where I sleep between shifts. I'm told it ought to be more.
b : Bare? | Nobody at all? | Ought it?
a : Bare is clean, and clean is everything. | Nobody but family and the dying. Both knock differently. | So I'm told. I've not found the hours to find out, #address#.

scene traveller_door
when topic=player
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a traveller about, asking questions. I've none to answer. | Strangers come to me when they're hurt, and that's when I'll see them. | I don't open #door# to a face I can't name, and a traveller's is a face I can't name.
b : You don't trust travellers? | Only then? | Never?
a : I trust what I can see, and I can't see a traveller's road. | Only then. Hurt is honest. A stranger at the door with a smile isn't. | Not after dark. By day I'll talk through the door, and that's generous, by me.

scene new_coughs
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : New folk in the street. I'll learn the coughs before I learn the names. | A newcomer came to #ward# with a cut and a long story. I treated the cut. | Somebody new by the corner. I've nothing against the newcomer, and nothing for, yet.
b : The coughs? | And the story? | Fair.
a : Everyone coughs in #city#. You can tell where a wolf's from by it. | Kept it. The story belonged to the patient, not to me. | Fair is all I give at first. The rest is earned, by measure.

scene thin_arms
when topic=times|health world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Lean weeks. #ward.capitalize# fills with folk sick from going hungry. Bread would do more than I can. | Lean, and it shows on #cots#. Thin arms, and colds that won't leave. | In lean times I see more burns. Folk crowd round one fire to save the coal.
b : Bread? | Won't leave? | Burns?
a : Bread, and a dry bed. I can give neither, and I can't cure hunger with #lint#. | Not till folk eat properly. I can only keep them warm on #cots#. | Paws and tails too near the coals. I've a salve for the burn, and none for the reason.

scene good_weeks_drunks
when topic=times world.times=good|boom
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Good weeks. Fewer hungry on #cots#, more drunks. The trade evens out. | Folk have coin, and spend it on #fish# and fighting. I see the fighting. | Times are good, they say. #cots.capitalize# don't know it yet.
b : Evens out? | And the fish? | Don't they?
a : It does. #city.capitalize# always finds a way to fill a cot. | I see that too, if I'm lucky, at #supper#. | Not yet. The poor feel good times last, and #sick# later still.

scene closed_mouth
when topic=gossip
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : People talk on a cot. I don't repeat a word of it. | I hear more than a priest does, and I keep it better. | Ask somebody else. What I hear on #ward# stays on the ward.
b : Not a word? | Better? | Fair enough.
a : Not one. A healer who talks is a healer nobody tells the truth to. | Better. A priest can forgive. I only forget, #very#. | It's how I sleep. It's how #sick# sleep, too.
b : #bc_fair# | #bc_wise# | #bc_true#

scene hurt_coming
when topic=gossip|crime topic.claim_kind=death|violence
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. If there's hurt in it, it'll come to #door#. | They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. #uneasy#.
b : Will it? | That's grim.
a : Most hurt does, sooner or later. I'll have #lint# ready. | Grim. Talking won't mend any of it; #lint# might.

scene wedding_crowd
when topic=gossip topic.claim_kind=marriage
does tell.gossip / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Good. A wedding is the only crowd I'm glad of. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim#, I hear. #gladnews#. I'll hope it lasts.
b : You don't like crowds? | It might.
a : At weddings, yes. Elsewhere crowds come back to me in pieces. | It might. I've seen worse matches mend, given time and #remedy#.

scene steady_paws
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I pray over #sick# when I'm asked. I'd rather they asked for boiled water too. | The Bright One sees to the end of it. I see to the start. | Steady paws are the Bright One's gift. I try not to waste them.
b : Both, then. | The start? | You don't waste them.
a : Both. Water first; a prayer goes better over #linen# that's clean. | The washing, the stitching, the waiting. The rest isn't mine to do. | I try. Some nights I'm not sure, #address#.

scene dream_pulse
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dream of #ward#, and I'm counting a pulse that won't stop. | I dream of the Waste at night, #cold#, full of stars, and nobody sick in it. | #tired.capitalize# wolves don't dream. I sleep like a stone and wake with the bell.
b : That sounds grim. | Nobody sick? | Lucky.
a : It isn't. A pulse that won't stop is a good dream, for a healer. | Nobody. I wake before I can enjoy it. | Lucky, or #tired#. One of the two.

scene slow_voice
when topic=accent self.away=yes here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #sick.capitalize# think I'm praying when I count. It's only a carter's rhyme from #self.from_town#. | A patient once asked where my slow voice came from. I said the Waste, and the patient slept better. | I say peace on you to the dying. City folk don't, and I think they ought to.
b : Does it matter? | Slept better? | They ought to?
a : Not to the pulse. It's the same rhyme in any tongue. | Better. A slow voice is half #remedy#. | They ought. It costs nothing, and the dying are owed it.

scene sump_stairs
when topic=work self.job=healer here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Every soul on #ward# comes up #stairs# on somebody's back. | #stairs.capitalize# cough louder than the Heights, but the cough is the same. | I go down #stairs# twice a week to see the ones who can't climb.
b : On somebody's back? | The same? | Twice a week?
a : Or on a door, if there's no back to spare. | The same. Only the Sump gets less sleep after. | Twice, and the rest by message. Nobody pays me for the stairs, #very#.

scene learner
when topic=work self.master=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody asked to learn the work. I said wash your paws in #basin# first, and see if you come back. | I'd take a learner who keeps a shut mouth and clean paws. #saying#. | Teaching is counting out loud. I'm better at counting quietly.
b : And did anyone come back? | Clean paws? | Out loud?
a : Not yet. Most don't, after the first #basin#. | Clean before the patient, clean after. Most forget the after. | Out loud, so the learner hears. I can't abide the sound of my own voice.

story caravan_count [topic=memories|lore self.from=saltwell self.age>=25]
  : An old carter taught me the counting rhyme, when I was a #child# hanging about the loads.
  : One well, two wells, the jar, the rope, the long road home. He counted his goats by it. I count hearts.
  ask : Have you a rhyme you count by?
  b : Only numbers. Yours sounds kinder.
  b[from=saltwell] : The same one. My grandfather sang it at the well.

story parted_rope [topic=memories self.age>=35]
  : My brother worked the cranes on #wharf# when I was new to this work.
  : A rope parted on a wet morning. I was there before anyone, and there was nothing to be done.
  : I learned that day that knowing what to do and being able to do it are two different roads.
  b : I'm sorry. That's a hard lesson.
  b[job=sailor] : I've seen a rope go. Nobody forgets it.

story own_paw [topic=work|memories self.job=healer self.age>=30]
  : The first wound I ever stitched was my own paw.
  : An old healer watched me do it and said nothing till the last knot, then said I'd do, and went back to the soup.
  ask : Has anyone ever told you, in so few words, that you'd do?
  b : Not in so few words.
  b[old] : Once. I've lived on it for years.

story long_road [topic=lore|pastimes self.likes=stars]
  : Carters call it the long road, that band of #skies# from the dunes to the far side.
  : Follow it, they say, and you'll find water by morning.
  : I've never tested it. I'd rather keep the story whole.
  b : Some stories are better kept.
  b[from=saltwell] : My grandmother walked by it once, and found the well.

story first_frost [topic=memories|weather self.away=yes self.likes=frosty_mornings here.region=ridgemere]
  : The first hard frost after I came down to #city#, #ward# went quiet.
  : No fevers, no fights. Everyone was too cold to quarrel.
  : I went out into the yard with my breath going up like smoke and thought: this city can be clean.
  b : Only for a morning.
  b[old] : Frost's the best healer there is, and it charges nothing.

rule @wash_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=healer
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Wash your paws. Then come in. | #basin.capitalize# first. Always the basin first.

rule @straw_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.likes=fresh_straw self.job=healer
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Old straw under this cot. Out with it. | #straw.capitalize#, and today, not tomorrow.

rule @gull_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=gulls here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Off, you screamer. | #annoyed#. #gulls.capitalize# on the roof again.

rule @night_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Quiet on #ward#. | Lamps down. Let #sick# sleep.

rule @star_bark
when concept=bark here.time=night here.outdoors=clear self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 12h
say There. The long road's out tonight. | #skies.capitalize# over #city#. #surprise#.

rule @feast_bark
when concept=bark world.festival=today
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #lint.capitalize#, #needle#, hot water. It's a feast. | #oath#. Feast day, and I'll see half of them before dawn.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Say what you need. | #greet#, #address#. Plainly, if you would.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Is anyone bleeding, or is it talk? | #topic.player#. I know your face. Go on, #address#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : #greet#. It's late. If it's a hurt, show me. If it's talk, be brief.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Stay where you are. #door.capitalize# opens for faces I can name, and yours isn't one yet.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=healer] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. #cots.capitalize#, #fever#, #straw#, #lint#: all of it mine to see to. | I keep #ward#. Wash, stitch, wait. Mostly wait.
dlg @2 resident.job : #work.capitalize#, whatever's in front of me, done properly. | I work, and say little about it. That's most of it.
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : #busy.capitalize#, which in my work is nothing to be glad of.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=failing] : Poorly, and no bandage hides it.
dlg @3 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : I keep no shop. #sick.capitalize# keep me, and there's never a shortage. | Steady. There's always someone on #cots#.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Word from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. I had it on #ward#.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : They're all talking of #world.event_words#. I'll see the end of it on a cot, likely.
dlg @3 resident.news [world.wagons=raided] : A wagon was stopped and stripped on the road. Stay inside the walls, if you've any sense.
dlg @4 resident.news [world.death=recent] : We lost one this week. I sat with the end of it. #rest#.
dlg @5 resident.news [world.wedding=recent] : There was a wedding. I hear the dancing went well, and only one brow split.
dlg @6 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# Coughs and colds, and those aren't news. | Nothing that's mine to tell, #address#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | What I hear on #ward# stays there.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. Past that, I've nothing.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Keep warm. | #farewell#. Keep any cut clean.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : #here.trade_title.capitalize#? Clean paws and a cold head, and the rest can be taught. Ask what you need. | You want to learn it. #learn_offer# Ask.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=no] : #hedge#, I've a learner already, and one is all I'll take. Ask what you like, even so.
dlg @1 master.work : Long nights, short words, and more waiting than anyone warns you of. #learn_offer# | Washing, mostly. Then stitching. Then waiting, and the waiting is hardest.
dlg @1 master.wages : No wage for a learner. You stand at my elbow and learn it thrice as fast as alone, and whatever you earn on your own is yours.
dlg @1 master.takes [here.take_on=yes] : I take only one, and only one I trust. You would do. Say the word.
dlg @2 master.takes [here.take_on=no] : Only one, and only one I trust. #here.take_on_why#
dlg @1 master.taken : Good. First light, paws washed, and stay near me. Say nothing to #sick# till I tell you. | #learn_taken#
dlg @1 master.refused : #topic.why# | Not yet. #topic.why#
dlg @1 master.bye : #farewell#. Wash your paws on the way out. | #farewell#, #address#.
graft resident.hub
choice What are you counting under your breath? -> rhyme
node rhyme
say A pulse, if there's one under my paw. The stars, if there isn't. It's an old carter's rhyme: one well, two wells, the jar, the rope, the long road home.
mood calm
free
choice Why that rhyme? -> rhyme_why
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node rhyme_why
say It keeps time better than I do, and I'd rather count than talk. That's all you'll get from me.
choice Fair enough. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft master.learn
choice What does a healer need most? [self.job=healer] -> need
node need
say Clean paws, a cold head, and patience for the night. The rest I can teach. Those three I can't.
mood stern
choice And if I faint at blood? -> need_blood
choice Tell me more. -> learn
node need_blood
say Then faint, get up, and wash your paws again. Everyone does it once. Nobody does it twice in front of me.
choice I'll remember. -> learn
choice Goodbye. -> bye
